Short:        Game Boy + Color emulator, AGA and RTG
Author:       Juan Antonio Gomez Galvez, Ville Helin, Ventzislav Tzvetkov, z00p
Uploader:     Zoopster (JCEC_1@yahoo.co.uk)
Type:         misc/emu
Version:      @VERSION@
Replaces:     misc/emu/AmiGameBoyCE.lha
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Requires:     AGA, 68020+ (68030/50 for mono, PiStorm-class for colour)
Distribution: Aminet

AmiGameBoy is a Game Boy and Game Boy Color emulator for AGA Amigas, in
68020+ assembly. It plays .gb and .gbc cartridges with sound, battery
saves and a CD32 pad, on the AGA screen or on a graphics board (RTG).
While a game runs it takes over the machine.

There are three programs:
  AGA       Game Boy and Game Boy Color on the AGA screen, for fast
            machines (PiStorm, BigMig, 68060 cards).
  AGA 030   Game Boy only, for an A1200 with a 68030/50.
  RTG       Game Boy and Game Boy Color on a 16-bit Picasso96 screen,
            with a screen surround.

History
-------
Juan Antonio Gomez Galvez began AmiGameBoy in 1996-97; his last public
version was 0.96. In 2026 he sent his sources for the community to carry
on. This community version, released with his consent, keeps his menu
and his AGA display and runs the games on the Game Boy engine of
Wzonka-Lad by Ville Helin and Ventzislav Tzvetkov (GPL-2).

2.1   Colour games in LCD colours by default ("Colours = Raw" for the
      colours as the game sets them); LCD Colours in the AGA and RTG
      Options menu, Bezel and Scanlines in the RTG one. Sound at the
      Game Boy's own balance (quieter). Final Fantasy Legend II and
      Mega Man V faster on a 68030/50. A pad test cartridge, PadTest.gb.
      Fixed: the light line at the left edge of the AGA picture, Dangan
      GB2's first stage.
2.0   Game Boy Color: the AGA and RTG programs play colour cartridges
      (colour-only and dual-mode). The RTG program draws on a graphics
      board, with a screen surround (Bezel), LCD blend and scanlines,
      each set in AmiGameBoy.config. Saves of up to 128 KB. CD32 pad:
      a steadier read, and "Pad = KTRL CD32+" for pads and adapters
      whose buttons flicker or drop out. Fixed: Infinity, Chantey's
      intro band, Last Crown Warriors' story pages. The Help page shows
      the pad layout in use; the menu cartridge info reads the whole
      header.
1.0   The Game Boy engine of Wzonka-Lad behind Juan's menu and display;
      four-channel sound on Paula; MBC1, MBC2, MBC3 and MBC5 cartridges
      with battery saves; CD32 pad with buttons set in AmiGameBoy.config;
      cartridges from the Shell or a project icon.

Requirements
------------
- An AGA Amiga with AmigaOS 3.0 or later.
- AGA 030: a 68020 or better; a 68030 at 50 MHz for full speed.
- AGA and RTG: a much faster machine (a PiStorm runs colour games at
  full speed). RTG also needs Picasso96 and a 16-bit screen mode.
- Memory: about twice the cartridge's size plus 256 KB.

Installation
------------
Unpack the archive anywhere. In the AmiGameBoy drawer start AGA, AGA
030 or RTG, choose Insert, pick a cartridge, then Power ON. Esc returns
to the menu. See ReadMe.txt or AmiGameBoy.guide for the keys, the pad,
the settings and the saves. Upgrading from 1.0: unpack over it. On a
68030/50 start AGA 030 from now on (AGA is now the colour program).
AmiGameBoy.config is kept; the RTG lines (Blend, Bezel, Scanlines) can
be added by hand, or delete the file to have it written again.

No games are included. You need cartridge images of your own, copies you
may legally have.

Not supported
-------------
Cartridges over 2 MB, the link cable, the Game Boy Camera and Printer,
Super Game Boy features. AGA 030 refuses colour-only cartridges and runs
dual-mode ones in mono.

